{"title":"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 13","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solutions</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the five-sided star shown, the letters <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are replaced by the numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, although not necessarily in that order. The sums of the numbers at the ends of the line segments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/0/ce0bfc603f9a044e308b1a1fdadca917e81ad2dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/9/699784c989c3db382520e6f92819e062d239f504.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{DE}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/3/f03a5d1a4c953313b40254abc33a95b7adabc9d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{EA}$\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> form an arithmetic sequence, although not necessarily in that order. What is the middle term of the arithmetic sequence?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/c/e7ccece18535f75fcce290018f4a4aecbfa38461.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(150); defaultpen(linewidth(0.8)); string[] strng = {&#39;A&#39;,&#39;D&#39;,&#39;B&#39;,&#39;E&#39;,&#39;C&#39;}; pair A=dir(90),B=dir(306),C=dir(162),D=dir(18),E=dir(234); draw(A--B--C--D--E--cycle); for(int i=0;i&lt;=4;i=i+1) { path circ=circle(dir(90-72*i),0.125); unfill(circ); draw(circ); label(&quot;$&quot;+strng[i]+&quot;$&quot;,dir(90-72*i)); } [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"242\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/8/2a8f88dd020315bc8e51f0b60ec9d78878263e77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\mathrm {A}) \\ 9 \\qquad (\\mathrm {B}) \\ 10 \\qquad (\\mathrm {C})\\ 11 \\qquad (\\mathrm {D}) \\ 12 \\qquad (\\mathrm {E})\\ 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"378\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solutions\">Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/f/a8ff6e790aa369050be53b3049bf8e4e28ab94d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(A+B) + (B+C) + (C+D) + (D+E) + (E+A) = 2(A+B+C+D+E)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"627\" height=\"20\" /> (i.e., each number is counted twice). The sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/b/79beafef51578909489be5664f582ce5b4e83385.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A + B + C + D + E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"161\" height=\"14\" /> will always be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/2/5f24b8065cb7c11a175d95c41dfdcf4ed966018d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 + 5 + 6 + 7 + 9 = 30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"176\" height=\"14\" />, so the arithmetic sequence has a sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/0/680df397231168ecac2d932d41fcde9aa4670da1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\cdot 30 = 60$\" width=\"82\" height=\"12\" />. The middle term must be the average of the five numbers, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/9/4f9454256f3cd04bddeedb06d390ade3ce5fa17c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{60}{5} = 12 \\Longrightarrow \\mathrm{(D)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"130\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let the terms in the arithmetic sequence be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/c/c2c117a4838e2be0c981f35f324153248f63e1ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/e/eaed2bcccb46f120de651287aca90d73b3c476db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + 2d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/8/f98014b8a564f6a2cafeab9787671fb9f1bc29e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + 3d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/b/62bf33e92e91c961e62cefa29a1d2a2ea7e08903.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + 4d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" />. We seek the middle term <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/e/eaed2bcccb46f120de651287aca90d73b3c476db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + 2d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>These five terms are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/b/c5bf77c6740d00af2866f26718d628a60c667ef2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A + B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/9/8c9d45b704ffb63f5e9284bb62220ddc955522e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B + C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/5/265656713bba48754d61c1d5bac40bf2c340ebfe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C + D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/0/7107ec9b1cfad062ed99dc987909aecef903d7d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D + E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/4/874bb320e89a302b02e0c0954b3ac05c76a7a878.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E + A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" />, in some order. The numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are equal to 3, 5, 6, 7, and 9, in some order, so\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/9/0b950e851b01fdef4121776d71bceb64dea71e98.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A + B + C + D + E = 3 + 5 + 6 + 7 + 9 = 30.\\]\" width=\"365\" height=\"14\" />\nHence, the sum of the five terms is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/b/96b4e29fc241c3a8aa1f8d21141905fb3dc1ea96.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(A + B) + (B + C) + (C + D) + (D + E) + (E + A) = 2A + 2B + 2C + 2D + 2E = 60.\\]\" width=\"586\" height=\"18\" />\nBut adding all five numbers, we also get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/9/c39d455b6de0d1bd8ae08a8b7406d04eedfc6393.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + (a + d) + (a + 2d) + (a + 3d) + (a + 4d) = 5a + 10d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"440\" height=\"18\" />, so\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/d/4ad7963ccb0acc510587c8046427c72115b6e099.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[5a + 10d = 60.\\]\" width=\"113\" height=\"14\" />\nDividing both sides by 5, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/2/3a2b77b30e5e1c37c0f4c1966987d71361c06642.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + 2d = \\boxed{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"104\" height=\"23\" />, which is the middle term. The answer is (D).\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Not too bad with some logic and the awesome guess and check. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/0/af04466ac38b7b0d0f451b3280c38f861ea13822.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" />. Then let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/d/1cd232b27c7bd446c8fa856ad08e6d166f3e09b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B=7,E=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"103\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/2/9324b954ba60afe9f4410f500208022a37d22b47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C=3,D=9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"104\" height=\"16\" />. Our arithmetic sequence is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/d/30d14acb631f41d1e4a8a87afcd0fe466317f4dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10,11,12,13,14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"123\" height=\"16\" /> so our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/3/4e3dbdf5abbcdadd27e735f1f3e93a934d920c51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12 \\Longrightarrow \\mathrm{(D)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Solution by franzliszt\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A\">2005 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017183101\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.056 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.076 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 343/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2298/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 9094/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   14.975      1 -total\n 62.54%    9.366      1 Template:AMC12_box\n 34.71%    5.198      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:5345:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017183101 and revision id 253024. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}